00:18:56.910 --> 00:19:20.310
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>I'd never heard of someone doing this-- MJ's system, using security cameras in your house to monitor kids doing remote school, while you have to go to work. It seemed extreme to me, but then I considered all the other arrangements and half-solutions I've heard parents devising to replace what school provided-- a free, dependable place to drop your kids.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>我从没听说过有人这样做——MJ的这套系统，用家里的安防摄像头监控远程学习的孩子，而自己不得不去工作。这对我来说似乎很极端，但随后我考虑了其他家长为了替代学校提供的免费、可靠的孩子看管地所采取的所有其他方案和权宜之计。

00:19:20.310 --> 00:19:44.970
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Parents who brought kids to their jobs at restaurants planted them at a table in the corner, while they worked their shift and hoped nobody in management asked, whose kid is that? Moms who put their children in empty hotel rooms to do remote school while they cleaned the other rooms down the hall. Parents who cut back on their hours or quit their jobs, took night shifts, so they could stay up all day with their kids doing Zoom school.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>把孩子带到餐厅工作、让他们坐在角落桌边的父母；妈妈们把孩子放在空酒店房间里远程学习，而自己在走廊的房间打扫卫生。缩减工时或辞职，改上夜班，以便白天能陪孩子上Zoom网课的父母。

00:19:44.970 --> 00:20:11.190
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Families that moved their entire lives to new cities that were cheaper or closer to a grandma who could look after the kids. MJ had a system that did not require her to depend on anyone else. The system was never late, or stuck in traffic, or sick, or too tired. It's kind of ingenious. School was not reliable. The system was entirely within her control.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>为了节省开支或离能照顾孩子的祖母更近一点，举家搬到新城市的家庭。MJ拥有一个不需要依赖任何人的系统。这个系统从不迟到、不堵车、不生病、也不疲劳。这很有创造力。学校并不可靠。这套系统完全在她的掌控之中。

00:20:11.190 --> 00:20:15.290
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Did you know other people who were doing this?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你认识其他这样做的人吗？

00:20:15.290 --> 00:20:37.320
<v MJ>No. I mean, if other moms are out there not wanting to say nothing, I get it. But, whew, there's not that panic of what so many other parents had to face that didn't have a system. I feel like I should do like an infomercial or something, you know-- (LAUGHING) for the system of security cameras and things like that.
<v MJ>没有。我的意思是，如果其他妈妈也在这样做但不愿提起，我明白。但是，呼，总比那些没有系统、面临恐慌的家长好多了。我觉得我应该做个广告什么的，你知道——（大笑）关于这套安防摄像头系统。

00:20:37.320 --> 00:20:38.090
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Yeah.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>是啊。

00:20:38.090 --> 00:20:43.160
<v MJ>I made it work. [LAUGHS] I made it work.
<v MJ>我想办法做到了。（大笑）我想办法做到了。

00:20:43.160 --> 00:20:53.300
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>And then, schools reopened. After 11 months of constant contact with her mom, zero separation, Neeah went back to a school building.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>后来，学校重新开放了。在与妈妈保持了11个月的密切联系、零分离之后，Neeah回到了校舍。

00:20:53.300 --> 00:21:01.890
<v Neeah>I had butterflies the entire time I was there. I'm like, oh, my god. What if I do something wrong? What if I get suspended today? And like, what if I don't make it through fourth grade?
<v Neeah>我在那里的时候一直很紧张。我就想，哦，我的天哪。如果我做错了什么怎么办？如果我今天被停学了怎么办？如果我四年级没读完怎么办？

00:21:01.890 --> 00:21:03.590
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Mm-hmm.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>嗯哼。

00:21:03.590 --> 00:21:08.450
<v Neeah>Just a whole day of butterflies, and--
<v Neeah>整天都在紧张，而且——

00:21:08.450 --> 00:21:09.410
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Yeah.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>是的。

00:21:09.410 --> 00:21:25.760
<v Neeah>Yeah, in the snap of a finger, I'm like, oh, crap. And my mom's not going to be here to be-- like, be here to watch over me, tell me to focus. Like, how am I going to do this? How am I going to do that without her telling me what to do? And that's when I started getting these panic attacks. Like--
<v Neeah>是的，转眼之间，我就想，噢糟了。我妈妈不会在这里了——在这里看着我，告诉我集中精神。我该怎么做？没有她告诉我该怎么做，我该怎么做那些事情？那时我就开始有这些恐慌症了。就像——

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:29.260
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>You started getting panic attacks when you went back to school?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你回到学校时就开始有恐慌症了吗？

00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:30.580
<v Neeah>Yeah.
<v Neeah>是的。

00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:31.900
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>I'm sorry to hear that.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>听到这个我很遗憾。

00:21:31.900 --> 00:21:54.340
<v Neeah>Mm-hmm. One of them was really bad, because I was in a panic attack for about 10, 15 minutes, because someone made me mad, really mad, kind of to the point where I started to cry a little bit. And then, I asked the substitute teacher if I can go to the bathroom. And then that's when it happened.
<v Neeah>嗯哼。其中一次真的很严重，因为我恐慌发作了大约10、15分钟，因为有人让我生气了，真的很生气，甚至到了我开始哭的地步。然后，我问代课老师我能不能去洗手间。就在那时发生了。

00:21:54.340 --> 00:22:09.590
<v Neeah>Like, I completely stopped. My heart stopped. My hands were shaking completely. I couldn't even talk. And then, thank god, this teacher, Ms. Murf let me sit in her room for a little bit, cool down, and go back to my room.
<v Neeah>我就完全停下来了。我的心跳停止了。我的手在颤抖，完全无法控制。我甚至说不出话。然后，谢天谢地，这位老师，Murf女士让我坐在她的办公室里待了一会儿，冷静一下，然后又回到了教室。

00:22:09.590 --> 00:22:27.160
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>You know, when you send a preschooler to their first day of school, that first big separation? And it's so hard, but you can never really know exactly what it's like for the kid, because they're so little. They can't really articulate it. But here is a fourth-grader who can.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你知道，当你送一个学龄前儿童去上第一天学，那种第一次重大分离？那真的很难，但你永远无法准确知道这对孩子来说意味着什么，因为他们太小了。他们无法准确表达。但这里有一个能表达的四年级学生。

00:22:27.160 --> 00:22:41.020
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Neeah says she missed knowing where her mom was. She missed her voice in the room. When things happened at school, when a kid said something mean, or she didn't understand the teacher, she wanted her mom there to take care of it, to protect her.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Neeah说她想念那种知道妈妈在哪里的感觉。她想念房间里妈妈的声音。当学校里发生事情时，当有孩子说刻薄的话，或者她听不懂老师讲课时，她希望妈妈在那里照看她，保护她。

00:22:41.020 --> 00:22:43.420
<v Neeah>Like, how I said she was talking a lot on the cameras?
<v Neeah>就像我说她在摄像头里经常说话一样？

00:22:43.420 --> 00:22:44.320
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Mm-hmm.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>嗯哼。

00:22:44.320 --> 00:22:57.880
<v Neeah>My life would be easier if she could see every move, everything that would happen, and know beforehand, and then contact somebody right away. But the world is not like that, so--
<v Neeah>如果妈妈能看到每一个动作、每一个发生的事情、提前知道，然后立刻联系某人，我的生活会更容易。但世界不是那样的，所以——

00:22:57.880 --> 00:23:02.740
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Yeah. Yeah, that's sort of part of growing up, I think.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>是的。是的，我想那是成长的一部分。

00:23:02.740 --> 00:23:11.770
<v Neeah>Mm-hmm. It would still be nice to hear her say, don't do this, don't do that, like it is in movies.
<v Neeah>嗯哼。如果能听到她说，别做这个，别做那个，就像电影里那样，还是挺好的。

00:23:11.770 --> 00:23:13.870
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Like, you mean a narrator in a movie?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你是说电影里的旁白？

00:23:13.870 --> 00:23:27.220
<v Neeah>Yeah. Yeah, like my mom would be the narrator of my head, and she'd tell me, make sure you ask questions, get the answers right, don't get distracted.
<v Neeah>是的。是的，就像我妈妈是我的大脑旁白，她会告诉我，一定要问问题，把答案答对，别分心。

00:23:27.220 --> 00:23:46.630
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>It's kind of what you hope happens with your kid, that your voice gets in their head and helps guide them through difficult stuff, but you know, a metaphorical voice in the head that eventually it becomes their own voice as they develop into their own people. Neeah had come to rely on a literal voice and just her mom's presence.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>这正是你希望在孩子身上发生的事情，他们的声音进入孩子的脑海，帮助引导他们度过困难的事情，但你知道，脑海中的隐喻声音，最终会随着他们成长为独立的个体，变成他们自己的声音。Neeah已经开始依赖真实的声音和她妈妈的存在。

00:23:46.630 --> 00:24:04.090
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Neeah heard from her mom so much during the day, through the cameras or on FaceTime, she missed knowing what her mom was up to at any given moment. She says it's actually what she missed most-- tracking her mom's day in parallel with her school day. It felt scary to lose that.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Neeah白天经常通过摄像头或FaceTime听到妈妈的声音，她想念那种能时刻知道妈妈在干什么的感觉。她说这实际上是她最想念的事情——在自己的学校生活同时追踪妈妈的一天。失去这种联系让人感到害怕。

00:24:04.090 --> 00:24:22.330
<v Neeah>I wish I could see and watch whatever she's doing. I'd want to see her, how hard she's working, or when people just don't give her anything to do. And then, just see what she eats for lunch-- if she eats lunch or breakfast-- because she doesn't really eat lunch or breakfast, because she doesn't get enough time to eat breakfast.
<v Neeah>我真希望我能看到并观察她正在做什么。我想看看她，她工作有多努力，或者当别人不给她安排任务时她在做什么。然后，看看她午饭吃什么——如果不吃午饭或早饭的话——因为她没有足够的时间吃早饭。

00:24:22.330 --> 00:24:23.950
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>You worry about her not eating?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你担心她没吃东西吗？

00:24:23.950 --> 00:24:29.150
<v Neeah>I do, because breakfast and lunch are probably the most important meals of the day.
<v Neeah>我担心，因为早饭和午饭可能是最重要的两餐。

00:24:29.150 --> 00:24:36.010
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>So if you could choose, you would like to have her watching you all the time and you watching her all the time?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>所以如果让你选择，你希望她一直看着你，你也一直看着她？

00:24:36.010 --> 00:24:39.350
<v Neeah>Yeah.
<v Neeah>是的。

00:24:39.350 --> 00:25:04.630
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>MJ, Neeah's mother, does not want this. What MJ wanted was to go back to how things were, where she'd drop Neeah at school and drive away, back to the time when school assumed responsibility for her child's safety and well-being. But once Neeah was back in school, MJ kept waiting for that feeling, the separation between parent life and work life, to set in.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Neeah的妈妈MJ并不想这样。MJ想要的是回到过去的状态，她会把Neeah送到学校然后开车离开，回到那个学校承担孩子安全和福利责任的时代。但在Neeah回到学校后，MJ一直在等待那种家长生活和工作生活分离的感觉产生。

00:25:04.630 --> 00:25:18.910
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>But it didn't. It felt different. First of all, Neeah was at a different school. Right before the pandemic, MJ bought a house, not far, but in a different school district. So that took getting used to, but there were other things.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>但这没有发生。感觉不同了。首先，Neeah在一所不同的学校。在大流行之前，MJ买了房子，离得不远，但在另一个学区。所以这需要时间适应，但还有其他事情。

00:25:18.910 --> 00:25:40.940
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Neeah bonded with her new teacher. And then suddenly, there was a substitute teacher, then another sub. Students got COVID. Teachers got COVID. Whole classrooms closed. Neeah's favorite teacher-- the art teacher, Ms. Gonzales-- quit. The next art teacher-- she quit, too. One day, MJ went to drop Neeah off at the bus stop.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Neeah和她的新老师建立了联系。然后突然之间，来了一位代课老师，然后又换了一位。学生得了新冠。老师得了新冠。整个教室关闭。Neeah最喜欢的老师——艺术老师Gonzales女士——辞职了。下一位艺术老师——也辞职了。有一天，MJ去接送Neeah上校车。

00:25:40.940 --> 00:25:55.480
<v MJ>It just didn't come. It didn't come one morning. The bus never came one morning. There was issues with subs. And I mean, I don't really know what their issues are, but it was a sub on both days. And you know, I'm at work.
<v MJ>它就是没来。有一天早上没来。校车有一天早上没来。代课老师有问题。我的意思是，我不知道他们有什么问题，但那两天是代课老师。而且你知道，我在工作。

00:25:55.480 --> 00:25:58.810
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>When she went to pick Neeah up after school--
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>当她放学后去接Neeah时——

00:25:58.810 --> 00:26:07.510
<v MJ>At the end of the day, I'm at the bus stop waiting for the bus. The bus came. She didn't get off the bus. I panicked.
<v MJ>一天结束时，我在校车站等校车。校车来了。她没下车。我慌了。

00:26:07.510 --> 00:26:11.020
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>What went through your head when she didn't get off the bus?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>当她没下车时，你脑子里闪过了什么？

00:26:11.020 --> 00:26:22.810
<v MJ>Just, it's instant, like, oh, my god-- just afraid. Like, I wouldn't even know where to begin to look for my daughter in the city. God forbid.
<v MJ>就是瞬间，比如，哦，我的天——只是恐惧。比如，我甚至不知道从哪里开始在这个城市寻找我的女儿。天哪，千万别发生那种事。

00:26:22.810 --> 00:26:39.520
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>The old way of doing school, the pre-pandemic way, felt different. MJ hated not knowing where Neeah was. She hated not seeing what was happening in the school building. The separation felt natural before, but now it felt agonizing.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>旧的教学方式，大流行之前的方式，感觉不同了。MJ讨厌不知道Neeah在哪里。她讨厌看不到校舍里发生的事情。以前分离感觉很自然，但现在感觉很痛苦。

00:26:39.520 --> 00:26:59.890
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Neeah would say there were fights at school. MJ wished she could see what happened. There was an incident with Neeah, another kid, and a marker. Another time, Neeah came home saying a boy touched her butt, and MJ was irate that it happened, but also that she didn't know it was happening, that the school hadn't called right away.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Neeah会说学校有打架事件。MJ希望她能看到发生了什么。Neeah和一个孩子以及一支记号笔发生了纠纷。另一次，Neeah回家说有个男孩摸了她的屁股，MJ对发生这种事感到暴怒，但更愤怒的是她竟然不知道，学校没有第一时间通知她。

00:26:59.890 --> 00:27:17.410
<v MJ>Whatever happens, happens. And then when they have all the information, then they want to call you. I want to know right away. Constant communication-- I don't care if you have to interrupt my day at work. If something is going on with my child, I need to know about it. Like, I'm in the loop.
<v MJ>发生什么就发生了。当他们掌握了所有信息，他们才想给你打电话。我想立刻知道。不断的沟通——我不在乎你是否必须打断我的工作。如果我的孩子发生了什么事，我需要知道。就像，我在关注中。

00:27:17.410 --> 00:27:28.840
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Yeah. Part of what seems like might be happening is that you had this year where you were deeply involved in every single thing Neeah did, and you watched. You were literally watching her.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>是的。看起来可能发生的一部分原因是，你有一年的时间深度参与了Neeah做的每一件事，而且你在看。你确实在看着她。

00:27:28.840 --> 00:27:29.740
<v MJ>Everything.
<v MJ>每一件事。

00:27:29.740 --> 00:27:35.530
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Yeah. And now, you have to trust this school and all these people in the school--
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>是的。而现在，你必须信任这所学校和学校里的所有人——

00:27:35.530 --> 00:27:37.870
<v MJ>That seems very incompetent, mm-hmm.
<v MJ>那看起来非常无能，嗯哼。

00:27:37.870 --> 00:27:42.810
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>--and a school system to do what you were doing.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>——以及一个学校系统来做你当时做的事情。

00:27:42.810 --> 00:28:02.620
<v MJ>Yeah. You know, it's very hard for my daughter to be in a new district, me to not have control, to not see her, but to not be in the loop of things. Yes, that is very hard. You know what I mean? It's like, oh, my god-- it's so frustrating. Since you are, like, at the end of my workday, I am about to order my lunch, so if you could just give me one second.
<v MJ>是的。你知道，我女儿在一个新学区，我没有控制权，我看不到她，无法掌握情况，这对她来说非常难。是的，这非常难。你懂我的意思吗？感觉就像，噢，我的天——这太令人沮丧了。既然你，也就是在我工作日结束的时候，我正准备点午餐，所以如果你能给我一秒钟的话。

00:28:02.620 --> 00:28:03.110
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>No problem.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>没问题。

00:28:03.110 --> 00:28:03.450
<v MJ>I'm so sorry.
<v MJ>我很抱歉。

00:28:03.450 --> 00:28:04.950
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Please-- no, eat. Eat.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>请——不，吃吧。吃吧。

00:28:04.950 --> 00:28:07.500
<v MJ>But I am starving.
<v MJ>但我饿坏了。

00:28:07.500 --> 00:28:16.310
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>MJ was grasping for a plan, calling the school repeatedly for help, not eating breakfast, as her daughter suspected.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>MJ一直在寻找计划，反复打电话给学校寻求帮助，没吃早饭，正如她女儿猜测的那样。

00:28:16.310 --> 00:28:34.480
<v MJ>[SIGHS] I feel like I just want to pull her, regardless, before I even have a plan. You know? I'm trying to mentally come up with a plan, while trying to work full-time and doing all this over-time. I'm trying, but it's like, oh, god, that's her school calling me right now.
<v MJ>（叹气）我觉得我还是想把她接走，不管怎样，甚至在我有计划之前。你知道吗？我正试图在脑子里想出个计划，同时还要做全职工作，做所有这些加班。我在努力，但感觉就像，哦，天哪，那是她学校现在正给我打电话。

00:28:34.480 --> 00:28:36.460
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Oh, go ahead. Call me back.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>哦，你忙你的。回头再打给我。

00:28:36.460 --> 00:28:36.980
<v MJ>OK, give me just--
<v MJ>好的，给我一点——

00:28:36.980 --> 00:28:37.540
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>OK. Take your time.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>好的。慢慢来。

00:28:37.540 --> 00:28:50.050
<v MJ>Give me one moment. OK. Hello?
<v MJ>给我一会时间。好的。喂？

00:28:50.050 --> 00:28:52.180
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Hey, MJ. It's Chana.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>嘿，MJ。是Chana。

00:28:52.180 --> 00:28:53.140
<v MJ>Hey, how are you?
<v MJ>嘿，你好吗？

00:28:53.140 --> 00:28:55.330
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Good. How have you been?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>好。你最近怎么样？

00:28:55.330 --> 00:28:57.430
<v MJ>No, I've been good. I've been real good.
<v MJ>不，我很好。我真的很好。

00:28:57.430 --> 00:29:10.600
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>This relaxed, breezy person is a mother who has her daughter back at home. In January, MJ pulled Neeah from school. The district is offering a virtual option, so Neeah is back online.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>这个放松、悠闲的人是一位让女儿回到身边的母亲。一月份，MJ让Neeah退学了。学区提供了虚拟选项，所以Neeah又回到了网上学习。

00:29:10.600 --> 00:29:16.450
<v MJ>Yeah. No, I'm not returning her [INAUDIBLE] with all the fifth graders-- all of fifth grade.
<v MJ>是啊。不，我没有让她回到那些五年级学生中间——所有五年级。

00:29:16.450 --> 00:29:20.050
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>So you're just kind of like, we're going to sit this whole thing out?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>所以你只是觉得，我们要避开这一切？

00:29:20.050 --> 00:29:21.400
<v MJ>Yeah, um--
<v MJ>是啊，嗯——

00:29:21.400 --> 00:29:24.730
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>For how long?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>多久？

00:29:24.730 --> 00:29:26.510
<v MJ>That's what I don't know.
<v MJ>那正是我不知道的。

00:29:26.510 --> 00:29:57.580
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>MJ told me, if the school situation did not improve, she'd consider remote school for the rest of Neeah's education. This is when I began to wonder if school, as we've known it, might be over. It's not only that MJ was questioning Neeah's school in all these new ways, it's that now, she could imagine an alternative. When something ever-present and unquestioned in your life disappears for a year, you learn it's not the only way to do things. And there's no unknowing that.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>MJ告诉我，如果学校的情况没有改善，她会考虑Neeah余下的教育都采取远程教育。这时我开始怀疑，我们所熟知的学校教育是否可能已经结束了。这不仅仅是因为MJ以各种新方式质疑Neeah的学校，而是现在，她可以想象出一种替代方案。当生活中一直存在且毫无疑问的事物消失一年后，你会意识到这不是唯一的做事方式。而且这种认知是无法抹去的。

00:29:57.580 --> 00:30:21.310
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Instead of returning to school, MJ and Neeah returned to the system. It was exactly the same, except for the school part. Neeah is in virtual school again, but this time it's not run by her public school. Neeah's school district did what an increasing number of public districts are now doing. They subcontracted a private company to provide an online remote-school option.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>MJ和Neeah没有回到学校，而是回到了“系统”。除了学校部分，其他一切都一样。Neeah又回到了虚拟学校，但这不再是由她的公立学校运营。Neeah的学区做了越来越多的公立学区现在正在做的事情。他们外包给一家私营公司来提供在线远程教学选项。

00:30:21.310 --> 00:30:36.490
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>The company provides an online platform and the curriculum. Neeah can go on, get all her lessons all by herself. She's not on Zoom. There's no teacher giving live instruction, and there's no classmates. She does everything alone, independently.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>这家公司提供在线平台和课程。Neeah可以自己上线，独自获取所有课程。她没开Zoom。没有老师进行实时授课，也没有同学。她一切都独自完成。

00:30:36.490 --> 00:30:50.590
<v Neeah>I just wake up in the morning. I get my hair done, get my teeth brushed, get dressed. I can do any subject I like, if I wanted to-- English, learning arts, math, PE, art.
<v Neeah>我早上起床。整理头发，刷牙，穿衣服。我可以做任何我想做的学科——英语、学习艺术、数学、体育、美术。

00:30:50.590 --> 00:30:52.860
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Do you miss having teachers?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你怀念老师吗？

00:30:52.860 --> 00:30:53.390
<v Neeah>No.
<v Neeah>不。

00:30:53.390 --> 00:30:54.160
<v Neeah>[MJ LAUGHS]
<v Neeah>（MJ大笑）

00:30:54.160 --> 00:30:55.870
<v Neeah>I don't.
<v Neeah>我不怀念。

00:30:55.870 --> 00:30:58.720
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>What if you don't understand the instructions?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>如果你看不懂说明书怎么办？

00:30:58.720 --> 00:31:03.820
<v Neeah>I can message the teacher, 'cause it gives me a little email box.
<v Neeah>我可以给老师发信息，因为它给了我一个小邮件框。

00:31:03.820 --> 00:31:20.810
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>She can email a teacher, but she rarely does. Neeah told me she likes that she can pace herself. She structures her own day. Sometimes, she starts at 8:00 AM, sometimes 9:00. Works for a couple hours, then has lunch. Watches Netflix, and just keeps going until she's done.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>她可以发邮件给老师，但她很少这样做。Neeah告诉我，她喜欢自己掌控进度。她安排自己的一天。有时她早上8点开始，有时9点。工作几个小时，然后吃午饭。看Netflix，一直做到结束。

00:31:20.810 --> 00:31:24.100
<v Neeah>I can just-- like, if it takes me all day, I'll do it all day.
<v Neeah>我可以——比如，如果它花掉我一整天，我就花一整天做。

00:31:24.100 --> 00:31:26.980
<v MJ>I would like for it to be done before I get home, though, you know?
<v MJ>但我希望它在我回家前完成，你知道吧？

00:31:26.980 --> 00:31:27.430
<v Neeah>I always get it done.
<v Neeah>我总是能完成。

00:31:27.430 --> 00:31:30.850
<v MJ>She shouldn't be in school while I'm getting home from work. But--
<v MJ>她不应该在我下班回家时还在上学。但是——

00:31:30.850 --> 00:31:32.980
<v Neeah>I'm usually done at, like, 12:00.
<v Neeah>我通常在12点左右做完。

00:31:32.980 --> 00:31:37.350
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Will you go a whole day without talking to anybody else?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你会整天不跟任何人说话吗？

00:31:37.350 --> 00:31:39.210
<v Neeah>Yeah.
<v Neeah>会。

00:31:39.210 --> 00:31:51.360
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>So you can get yourself up at 7:00 in the morning, do your work yourself, take your break, watch TV, go back to doing your work, finish your schoolwork, and get to the end of the day without talking to anybody?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>所以你可以早上7点起床，自己做功课，休息，看电视，回去做功课，完成学业，直到一天结束都不跟任何人说话？

00:31:51.360 --> 00:32:00.960
<v Neeah>Um, no. 'Cause every time I wake up in the morning, I'm like, I'm going to call Mom, make sure she's OK, make sure she got to work safely.
<v Neeah>嗯，不会。因为每次早上起床，我都想，我要给妈妈打个电话，确保她没事，确保她安全到达工作地点。

00:32:00.960 --> 00:32:05.090
<v MJ>She calls me, literally, every day, every morning.
<v MJ>她确实，字面意义上，每天、每天早上都给我打电话。

00:32:05.090 --> 00:32:23.570
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Is this school? It lacks every element I might have said defines what school is. She doesn't go to a building. There's no teaching, no schedule, no classmates. That's the part I couldn't get over. No kids. The only person Neeah talks to all day is her mom.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>这是学校吗？它缺乏我可能认为定义学校的所有要素。她不去建筑，没有教学，没有课程表，没有同学。那是我无法克服的部分。没有孩子。Neeah整天说话的唯一对象就是她妈妈。

00:32:23.570 --> 00:32:40.710
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>That part worries MJ, that Neeah's missing everything about school that mattered most to MJ as a kid. MJ says school's where I figured out who I was. It's where I learned I'm not the prettiest girl, but the fastest on field day. It's where she learned when to fight, how to apologize.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>MJ担心这一部分，担心Neeah错过了作为孩子时对MJ最重要的一切。MJ说学校是我发现自我身份的地方。在那里我学会了我不是最漂亮的女孩，但我是运动会上跑得最快的。在那里她学会了何时反击，如何道歉。

00:32:40.710 --> 00:32:54.620
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>It's where she made her best friends, lifelong friendships, she says, of 26-plus years. She's worried Neeah is missing all of that. But Neeah sounds pretty settled, like she'd finally arrived.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>在那里她交到了最好的朋友，她说那是26年以上的终身友谊。她担心Neeah错过了这一切。但Neeah听起来很满足，好像她终于到达了目的地。

00:32:54.620 --> 00:32:58.550
<v Neeah>Total peace and quiet is my kind of thing.
<v Neeah>绝对的平静和安静是我喜欢的东西。

00:32:58.550 --> 00:33:18.390
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>When Neeah takes a break or finishes her online work, she sits on the couch at home, and she watches her favorite show on Netflix-- Alexa and Katie. It's a wholesome sitcom about two best friends. One gets cancer, but survives. And now, they're heading to high school for the first time, choosing their first-day-of-school outfits. Will they have the same lunch period?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>当Neeah休息或完成在线工作时，她坐在家里的沙发上，观看她最喜欢的Netflix剧集——《亚历克萨与凯蒂》。这是一部关于两个好朋友的健康情景喜剧。一个患了癌症，但活了下来。现在，她们第一次进入高中，挑选开学第一天的行头。她们会有同样的午餐时间吗？

00:33:18.390 --> 00:33:25.350
<v Katie>Everyone, get out your school schedules. One, two, three.
<v Katie>所有人，拿出你们的学校时间表。一，二，三。

00:33:25.350 --> 00:33:29.400
<v Alexa>I'm Alexa, and this is my best friend, Katie. We're about to start high school.
<v Alexa>我是亚历克萨，这是我最好的朋友凯蒂。我们马上要开始上高中了。

00:33:29.400 --> 00:33:32.130
<v Katie>Oh, my gosh. That's in three days.
<v Katie>天哪。那还有三天。

00:33:32.130 --> 00:34:02.310
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>This is what Neeah's watching from her dystopian cyber school surveillance state. She's watching school. When Takeru Nagayoshi, the Teacher of the Year, who we heard from at the beginning of this show, told me pre-pandemic school was a bygone era, I think this is what that looks like-- Neeah watching school alone in her home, with cameras watching her.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>这就是Neeah在她的反乌托邦网络学校监控状态下观看的内容。她在看“学校”。当年度教师Takeru Nagayoshi在节目开头对我说大流行前的学校是一个逝去的时代时，我想这就是它的样子——Neeah独自在家里看着学校，同时摄像头看着她。

00:34:02.310 --> 00:34:23.130
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>That's where this story was going to end. But last week, as I was putting it together, I got one more message from MJ. She said she learned Neeah had not been submitting assignments in her online school. Turns out a teacher-less outsourced program with no actual person-to-person interaction did not work. Or at least, it didn't work for Neeah.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>故事本该到此结束。但上周，在我整理它时，我收到了MJ的一条信息。她说她得知Neeah没有在网校提交作业。事实证明，没有实际人与人互动的教师外包项目根本没用。或者至少，对Neeah没用。

00:34:23.130 --> 00:34:48.440
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>MJ was deeply deflated. Her system had failed, and the school system had failed, too. She told me she'd decided to send Neeah back to school in person, for now. That is, until she figures out what's next.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>MJ感到非常泄气。她的系统失败了，学校系统也失败了。她告诉我，她决定让Neeah先回到学校上课。至少，直到她想出下一步怎么办。

00:34:48.440 --> 00:35:05.450
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Coming up, a kid who disappeared from school a year and a half ago shows up again and tries to just blend in. That's in a minute from Chicago Public Radio when our program continues.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>接下来，一个一年半前从学校消失的孩子再次出现，并试图融入其中。那是芝加哥公共广播电台在我们的节目继续时带来的内容。

00:35:05.450 --> 00:35:30.470
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>It's This American Life. I'm Chana Joffe-Walt, sitting in for Ira Glass. At the show this year, we've been talking a lot about a feeling we've all noticed around us-- a feeling of unraveling. We're doing a couple of episodes about people who are facing things that feel like they're coming apart in front of them. Like, we did a show a couple of weeks ago about cities and towns becoming unlivable with climate change.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>这是《美国生活》。我是Chana Joffe-Walt，代替Ira Glass主持。今年在节目中，我们一直在谈论一种我们在周围都注意到的感觉——一种解体的感觉。我们正在制作几集关于人们面对那些感觉正在他们面前分崩离析的事物的节目。就像几周前我们做了一期关于气候变化让城镇变得不适合居住的节目。

00:35:30.470 --> 00:35:55.460
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>This episode is also about that feeling, a slow-moving unraveling in schools. We are now in the third consecutive school year disrupted by COVID-- disruptions that have at times undone even the most basic foundational part of what school is, like the idea that kids go to school every day. Attendance is down. Enrollment is down.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>这一集也是关于那种感觉，学校里缓慢进行的解体。我们现在处于因新冠疫情而中断的连续第三个学年——这些中断有时甚至撤销了学校最基本、最基础的部分，比如孩子们每天上学的理念。出勤率下降了。入学率下降了。

00:35:55.460 --> 00:36:26.720
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>I remember back when schools first closed two years ago, there were kids who just disappeared. I saw a report in the fall of 2020 that estimated three million kids were out of touch with school. A principal in Los Angeles, Vanessa Garza, told me about one of them-- a student they completely lost track of when schools closed in March 2020. And then a month into this school year, I was talking with Principal Garza on the phone, and she says, oh, that girl who disappeared back in spring 2020--
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>我记得两年前学校刚关闭时，有些孩子直接消失了。我在2020年秋天看到一份报告估计有300万孩子与学校失去联系。洛杉矶的一位校长Vanessa Garza告诉了我其中一个——一个在2020年3月学校关闭时完全失去踪迹的学生。而在这一学年开始一个月后，我和Garza校长通了电话，她说，哦，那个2020年春天消失的女孩——

00:36:26.720 --> 00:36:32.240
<v Principal Garza>Literally, yesterday, that student and her family just re-enrolled with us.
<v Principal Garza>就在昨天，那个学生和她的家人重新向我们注册了。

00:36:32.240 --> 00:36:33.920
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Just yesterday?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>就在昨天？

00:36:33.920 --> 00:36:55.520
<v Principal Garza>Exactly. You know, I'd like to come back. We're like, great. Let's get a copy of your records. Where were you? What school were you at, so I can request them? And they're like, I didn't go to school. So in the time that the pandemic started and shut down our schools, March 13, 2020, till now, that student hasn't been in school.
<v Principal Garza>确切地说。你知道，我很高兴回来。我们说，太好了。让我们拿一份你的记录。你在哪儿？你在哪所学校，我好去调取？他们说，我没上学。所以从大流行开始并关闭我们学校的2020年3月13日到现在，那个学生一直没上学。

00:36:55.520 --> 00:37:09.740
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>She never finished sixth grade, missed all of seventh grade. And now here she was, a month into her eighth-grade school year, ready to return. This kid-- I'm going to call her Maricela. That's not her real name.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>她从未读完六年级，错过了整个七年级。而现在她来了，在八年级开学一个月后，准备回来了。这个孩子——我叫她Maricela。那不是她的真名。

00:37:09.740 --> 00:37:29.550
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Her mom told me I could meet her at school for one of her first days back, which I really wanted to, because I'd always wanted to know, what were kids who were not in school doing all that time? Literally, like, what was she doing with her time? What were her days like for the last year and a half? And what would it be like to come back to school?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>她妈妈告诉我，我可以在她回校的头几天里在学校见她，我真的很想，因为我一直想知道，那些不上学的孩子在那段时间里都在干什么？字面意思，她用时间干了什么？过去一年半她的日子是怎么过的？回到学校会是什么样子？

00:37:29.550 --> 00:37:34.340
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>So that is Act Two, The Case of the Vanishing Sixth Grader.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>所以这是第二幕，消失的六年级学生案。

00:37:34.340 --> 00:37:35.210
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Good morning.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>早上好。

00:37:35.210 --> 00:37:36.920
<v Principal Garza>Hi. Good morning.
<v Principal Garza>嗨。早上好。

00:37:36.920 --> 00:37:59.750
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>I'm waiting in the hallway with Principal Vanessa Garza at the Girls' Athletic Leadership School, GALS. It's a charter school in Los Angeles, one of those California schools where lots of stuff happens outside next to palm trees. Almost all the students are Latina, some from transnational families that will travel back and forth to family in Mexico or Central America for holidays.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>我正和洛杉矶女子领导力学校（GALS）的校长Vanessa Garza在走廊里等待。这是一所位于洛杉矶的特许学校，是那种加州学校之一，很多活动都在棕榈树旁边的室外进行。几乎所有的学生都是拉美裔，有些来自在墨西哥或中美洲有家庭、假期会往返的跨国家庭。

00:37:59.750 --> 00:38:16.130
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Sometimes, students who have just moved to LA from those places show up at GALS. But a kid who's been missing for 18 months-- that is not common. Principal Vanessa Garza is eagerly scanning the hallway, looking for Maricela. Is she actually going to show?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>有时，刚从那些地方搬到洛杉矶的学生会出现在GALS。但是一个失踪了18个月的孩子——那并不常见。Vanessa Garza校长正热切地扫描着走廊，寻找Maricela。她真的会来吗？

00:38:16.130 --> 00:38:20.180
<v Principal Garza>Fingers crossed. It's almost 7:30 right now. [LAUGHS]
<v Principal Garza>祈祷。现在快7点半了。（大笑）

00:38:20.180 --> 00:38:28.400
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>We turned to see another staff member hustling down the hall toward us, silently waving her arms and mouthing, she's here!
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>我们转头看到另一名工作人员正匆忙地向我们走来，默默挥动手臂，口型说着，她来了！

00:38:28.400 --> 00:38:32.270
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>She's here? Yay! All right.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>她来了？耶！好的。

00:38:32.270 --> 00:38:43.130
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>The second Maricela walked into the building, I felt like, OK, I'm finally going to get my answer. Where has she been? What happened? And what's it like to be back here?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Maricela走进大楼的那一刻，我感觉，好吧，我终于要得到答案了。她去哪了？发生了什么？回到这里是什么感觉？

00:38:43.130 --> 00:38:57.890
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>But she's kind of like a famous person right now, so I had to wait my turn. She enters the hallway to the school, and immediately gets sort of trapped between the bathroom, the main office, and her principal, who can barely contain her excitement.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>但她现在有点像个名人了，所以我必须排队等候。她进入通往学校的走廊，立刻被困在洗手间、教务办公室和几乎无法抑制兴奋的校长之间。

00:38:57.890 --> 00:39:04.490
<v Principal Garza>Good morning! How are you? Did you get a chance to get breakfast?
<v Principal Garza>早上好！你好吗？有机会吃早饭了吗？

00:39:04.490 --> 00:39:21.770
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Maricela's got long, straight, black hair parted in the middle, gray leggings, and a red JanSport backpack. She's barely audible, arms at her chest. She looks like she'd very much like to make herself smaller, less visible, but her overeager host keeps offering her things.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Maricela留着中分的长直黑发，穿着灰色紧身裤，背着一个红色的JanSport背包。她几乎听不见声音，双臂抱在胸前。她看起来很想让自己变得更小、更不显眼，但她那位过于热情的接待者一直在给她东西。

00:39:21.770 --> 00:39:43.430
<v Principal Garza>Do you want to grab something that you can save for later? Because it's just coffee cake. You're good? OK. You're in Ms. Elaina's wellness team, right? All right, so let's walk over there and check in with Ms. Elaina. And then, I'll get you a fresh mask, too. It looks like that one is well-loved, right? [CHUCKLES]
<v Principal Garza>想拿点可以留着以后吃的东西吗？因为只是咖啡蛋糕。你饱了吗？好的。你在Elaina女士的健康小组对吧？好的，那我们走过去和Elaina女士报到一下。然后，我会给你一个新口罩，看起来那个已经很旧了，对吧？（轻笑）

00:39:43.430 --> 00:40:03.620
