<v Maricela>Yeah. I don't really like it, 'cause I don't like to be, like, locked up.
<v Maricela>是的。我真的不喜欢那样，因为我不喜欢被关起来。

00:45:09.820 --> 00:45:13.380
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>And what did you do all day?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你整天都在做什么？

00:45:13.380 --> 00:45:31.620
<v Maricela>Um, we had to stay in the-- I had a computer over there, a touchscreen computer. I would play Roblox on there, or watch videos, or do whatever I wanted to do. And my sister had her iPad. And I had a TV, and my brother would use the TV.
<v Maricela>嗯，我们必须待在——我那边有一台电脑，一台触摸屏电脑。我会在上面玩Roblox，或者看视频，或者做任何我想做的事。我妹妹有她的iPad。我有一台电视，弟弟会用那台电视。

00:45:31.620 --> 00:45:52.890
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Screens, a lot of screens. Of course. What were millions of missing kids up to when school buildings closed? Playing Roblox. I don't know what I expected. But talking to Maricela and hearing her lay out what happened over those 18 months she was absent from school, it did feel like such an interior, specific view.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>屏幕，很多的屏幕。当然。当校舍关闭时，数百万失踪的孩子都在忙什么？玩Roblox。我不知道我期待什么。但和Maricela交谈并听她讲述她在缺席学校的那18个月里发生的事情，确实感觉像是一个如此内在、具体的视角。

00:45:52.890 --> 00:46:05.430
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>I'd been thinking about this as a story of a kid who disappeared from school. But of course, that's not Maricela's story about herself. In Maricela's telling, she didn't disappear, school disappeared.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>我一直认为这是一个孩子从学校消失的故事。但当然，那不是Maricela关于她自己的故事。在Maricela的讲述中，她没有消失，学校消失了。

00:46:05.430 --> 00:46:36.870
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>So much of our conversation about schools right now, our ideas about what schools need, what needs to happen to help kids catch up, to get back to normal, usually comes from the perspective of teachers, parents, adults. I want you to hear Maricela's version of this, to hear what it's been like for one of the millions of kids during the pandemic who just stopped attending school-- all the details that matter to her, the stuff that is at eye-level to a kid, stuff adults don't always think to focus on.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>我们目前关于学校的对话中，关于我们认为学校需要什么、需要发生什么来帮助孩子赶上进度、恢复正常的所有想法，通常都来自老师、家长和成年人的视角。我想让你们听听Maricela的版本，听听在大流行期间数百万停止上学的孩子之一的经历——所有对她重要的细节，那些处于孩子视线水平的东西，成年人并不总是想到去关注的东西。

00:46:36.870 --> 00:46:56.430
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>It was not a blip for Maricela, it was epic. A lot happened. First, her mom lost her job. Then, her grandparents got sick. And while they were in Mexico, they lost their apartment in Los Angeles. The manager said they'd abandoned it. When they came back to Los Angeles, Maricela's aunt said they could stay with her.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>对于Maricela来说，这不是一个“闪现”，这是史诗级的。发生了太多的事情。首先，她妈妈失业了。然后，爷爷奶奶病了。当他们在墨西哥时，他们在洛杉矶的公寓没了。经理说他们遗弃了公寓。当他们回到洛杉矶，Maricela的阿姨说他们可以住在她家。

00:46:56.430 --> 00:47:23.780
<v Maricela>We all had our schedules, like, who does this, who does that. For example, like, we would wake up, and we would sleep in the living room. We would pick up, we would vacuum the whole living room. We would have to wash the dishes, cook, and then wash those dishes, and broom the kitchen, clean the table after we're done eating, and then clean the bathroom, if it's dirty.
<v Maricela>我们都有自己的时间表，谁干这个，谁干那个。例如，我们起床，住在客厅。我们要清理，我们整个客厅都要吸尘。我们要洗碗、做饭，然后洗碗，扫厨房，吃完饭清理桌子，然后清洁卫生间，如果它脏了的话。

00:47:23.780 --> 00:47:34.880
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Her cousins' kids, though, her aunt's kids-- Maricela says they hardly did anything. She's the oldest in her family. It's her and a younger brother and sister. So a lot of the chores fell to her. It wasn't fair.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>她表亲的孩子们，她阿姨的孩子，Maricela说他们几乎什么都不做。她是家里最大的。她还有一个弟弟和一个妹妹。所以大量的家务落在了她身上。这不公平。

00:47:34.880 --> 00:47:45.290
<v Maricela>And I couldn't tell them anything, because they're snitches. And they told their parents everything about what they do. So I would just ignore it.
<v Maricela>我不能告诉他们什么，因为他们是告密者。他们把做什么都告诉了父母。所以我只能忽视它。

00:47:45.290 --> 00:48:02.300
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>It got tense in the apartment. And sometime in the middle of what would have been Maricela's seventh-grade school year, her family moved into their truck. They'd drive to the park she always played at and grab a spot every night. In the daytime, they had a routine. Her younger brother and sister would sleep in the back.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>公寓里的气氛变得紧张。在Maricela原本应该是七年级学年的中间某段时候，她家搬进了卡车。他们每天晚上都会开车去她一直玩的公园找个地方停。白天，他们有日常规律。她的弟弟妹妹会在后面睡觉。

00:48:02.300 --> 00:48:17.180
<v Maricela>They would wake up, like, around 9:00. We would go get breakfast while they were sleeping. We would wake-- we would go park at the park again, and then they would wake up. We would fix the seats, and then they would sit down and eat breakfast.
<v Maricela>他们会在9点左右起床。我们在他们睡觉时去买早饭。我们会——我们会再去公园停好车，然后他们会醒来。我们整理好座位，然后他们坐下来吃早饭。

00:48:17.180 --> 00:48:19.400
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>And then, what would happen? What would you do the rest of the day?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>然后，发生了什么？那天剩下的时间你做什么？

00:48:19.400 --> 00:48:40.310
<v Maricela>And then, we would go to my mom's-- to my cousin's house, and we would shower there. We had bathrooms at the park. And to brush our teeth, we'd just brush them like-- we would go to the bathroom, take a water bottle, toothpaste, and my toothbrush, and we would brush them in there.
<v Maricela>然后，我们去我妈妈的——我表亲家，在那里洗澡。我们在公园有卫生间。刷牙时，我们就——去洗手间，拿个水瓶、牙膏和牙刷，在里面刷牙。

00:48:40.310 --> 00:48:52.970
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>I talked to Maricela's mom. She confirmed the basics. She lost her job when the pandemic hit, the apartment. They went to Mexico to care for her folks. But she didn't want to do an interview or get into any of this in detail.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>我跟Maricela的妈妈聊过。她证实了基本情况。大流行来袭时她失业了，公寓也没了。他们去墨西哥照顾她的父母。但她不想接受采访或深入详细讨论这一切。

00:48:52.970 --> 00:49:12.590
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>So I don't know much about where her head was at or what shaped all the different choices she had to make during that time. She wanted to let Maricela share her experience. When they were staying in the truck, Maricela's mom called LA Family Housing. A caseworker got them a place in a hotel. That's where they're living now.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>所以我不知道她的心思在哪里，或者在那段时间里塑造她所做的不同选择的是什么。她想让Maricela分享她的经历。当他们住在卡车里时，Maricela的妈妈给洛杉矶家庭住房中心打了电话。一位个案工作者帮他们在一家酒店找到了住处。那是他们现在住的地方。

00:49:12.590 --> 00:49:38.480
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>And then, the caseworker asked where Maricela wanted to register for school. I don't know if she asked or if she told her she had to. GALS is 40 minutes, in traffic, from the hotel. Maybe somewhere closer, she asked? No, Maricela said. She'd prefer to go back to the school she knows.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>然后，个案工作者问Maricela想去哪里注册学校。我不知道她是问她还是告诉她必须去。GALS在交通堵塞时距离酒店有40分钟车程。或者找个近点的地方？不，Maricela说。她宁愿回到她熟悉的学校。

00:49:38.480 --> 00:50:05.210
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>It's funny, when you think about it, that very basic idea that school is where you go as a kid, the thing the rest of life revolves around, it took centuries to establish. It took laws, and social movements, and fiery speeches to establish a sprawling compulsory public education system. But it only took a few months-- weeks, even, with Maricela-- for that idea to be completely undone.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>想想看真是有趣，那个最基本的想法——学校是孩子去的地方，是生活围绕运行的东西，它花了几百年才建立起来。它花费了法律、社会运动和火热的演讲才建立起庞大的义务公共教育系统。但它只花了几个月——用Maricela的例子甚至只有几周时间——这个理念就完全被撤销了。

00:50:05.210 --> 00:50:21.860
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>And when it was, when school disappeared from Maricela's life, all the other things-- more immediate, huge dramas-- came in and filled the space. Her mom lost her job. They lived in a truck. She sold candy in the park. Her cousins were snitches. Her family died.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>当学校从Maricela的生活中消失时，所有其他事物——更直接、巨大的戏剧——进来了并填补了空间。她妈妈失业了。他们住在卡车里。她在公园卖糖果。她的表亲是告密者。她的家人去世了。

00:50:21.860 --> 00:50:39.170
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>She can talk about all of that for hours. But when I asked Maricela, what about school, she just sort of drifts to some other topic. Not that she doesn't want to talk about it, it almost felt like she didn't remember when the pandemic closed schools. It didn't register.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>她可以谈论所有这些长达数小时。但当我问Maricela学校怎么样时，她只是漂移到其他话题上。并不是说她不想谈论它，几乎感觉她记不清大流行什么时候关闭了学校。没注册上。

00:50:39.170 --> 00:50:42.300
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>What did you do in sixth grade when schools closed?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>六年级学校关闭时你干什么了？

00:50:42.300 --> 00:50:50.210
<v Maricela>Um, in sixth grade, when school closed, I didn't finish sixth grade.
<v Maricela>嗯，六年级学校关闭时，我没读完六年级。

00:50:50.210 --> 00:51:00.590
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Why? I would ask, over and over. They closed schools, she'd say. But what about online school? No. Why? I don't know.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>为什么？我会一遍又一遍地问。他们关闭了学校，她说。但在线学校呢？不。为什么？我不知道。

00:51:00.590 --> 00:51:05.720
<v Maricela>It was-- because I wasn't in school at that time.
<v Maricela>是因为我那时候没上学。

00:51:05.720 --> 00:51:09.980
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Why weren't you in school at that time?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>那时候你为什么没上学？

00:51:09.980 --> 00:51:12.200
<v Maricela>I don't know.
<v Maricela>我不知道。

00:51:12.200 --> 00:51:15.140
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Did you want to be in school?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你想上学吗？

00:51:15.140 --> 00:51:20.360
<v Maricela>No. Because I knew that I couldn't hang out with Valeria.
<v Maricela>不想。因为我知道我没法和Valeria一起玩了。

00:51:20.360 --> 00:51:36.150
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Valeria. Valeria was Maricela's best friend at school. She lived in her building. The vague fog Maricela has when I ask her about school evaporated instantly when the conversation turned to Valeria in sixth grade.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Valeria。Valeria是Maricela在学校最好的朋友。她住在她那栋楼。当我问她关于六年级的事时，Maricela那种模糊的迷雾在谈话转到六年级的Valeria身上时瞬间消失了。

00:51:36.150 --> 00:52:00.710
<v Maricela>No, I met her-- OK, so when she came from Mexico, she would, like, go to my house a lot. We lived in the same building, and she would go, like, at 6:00 in the morning, and we would come on our way to school together. And we were, like, really close friends that-- this one time, she was knocking at my door, and I opened it, and then we made breakfast together, and then we served--
<v Maricela>不，我认识她——好的，当她从墨西哥来的时候，她会经常去我家。我们住在同一栋楼，她会在早上6点去我家，我们一起去学校。我们是非常亲密的朋友——有一次，她在敲我的门，我打开门，然后我们一起做早餐，然后我们准备了——

00:52:00.710 --> 00:52:19.710
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Maricela became so specific when she talked about Valeria, in that kid way where she's living it in real time, where every detail of a story is shared and assigned exactly equal weight. She knocked. I opened the door. We made breakfast. Here's who came. Here's where we sat. Here's what we ate.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Maricela在谈到Valeria时变得如此具体，用那种孩子般的方式——活在当下，分享每一个故事的每一个细节，并给予完全平等的重视。她敲门。我开门。我们做早餐。谁来了。我们坐在哪。我们吃什么。

00:52:19.710 --> 00:52:34.580
<v Maricela>--like a tortilla. And then you crack an egg on top. And then, we sliced, like, tomatoes and onions, and we put it on the top. She went to her house, and she got clothes. And she showered in my mom's bathroom while I showered in mine. And then--
<v Maricela>——像玉米饼。然后你在上面敲个蛋。然后，我们切西红柿和洋葱放在上面。她去她家拿衣服。她在妈妈的浴室洗澡，我在我的浴室洗澡。然后——

00:52:34.580 --> 00:52:43.640
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>They went out walking, and they ran into Maricela's aunt, who gave her some cash. They went to the store. Maricela snuck to the side and bought something special.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>她们走路出去，遇到了Maricela的阿姨，给了她一些现金。她们去商店。Maricela偷偷溜到一边买了特别的东西。

00:52:43.640 --> 00:52:50.930
<v Maricela>They were, like, little silver hearts that come apart, and they said, "best friends."
<v Maricela>它们是那种能分开的小银心，上面写着“最好的朋友”。

00:52:50.930 --> 00:52:54.140
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Like one of those best-friend hearts, broken heart?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>就像那种心碎的最好朋友钥匙扣？

00:52:54.140 --> 00:53:13.190
<v Maricela>Yeah, but it was like a keychain thing, and we both had it, like, on our backpack. And when we came to the school both together, we were, like, so close. And we would hang out with the other girls, but there was, like, always a space with the other girls.
<v Maricela>是的，但这就像一个钥匙扣，我们都在背包上挂着。当我们一起去学校时，我们非常亲密。我们会和其他女孩一起玩，但和其他女孩相处时总是有一点空间。

00:53:13.190 --> 00:53:26.860
<v Maricela>But me and her were, like, always next to each other. We were, like, really best friends. And then, we would go to the bathroom, and she would wait for me, like, outside the stall. And then she would go in, and I would wait for her.
<v Maricela>但我跟她一直挨着。我们是非常好的朋友。然后我们会去洗手间，她会在隔间外等我。然后她进去，我等她。

00:53:26.860 --> 00:53:48.400
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>March 2020, schools closed and upended the lives of millions of families. But again, that's not what Maricela remembers of this time. March 2020, the day before Maricela went to Mexico, what she remembers is that she had a picnic with Valeria at the Valley Plaza Park. Their families came. They ate Pollo Loco.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>2020年3月，学校关闭，颠覆了数百万家庭的生活。但再次强调，这不是Maricela记忆中那段时光。2020年3月，Maricela去墨西哥的前一天，她记得是在Valley Plaza公园和Valeria野餐。她们的家人也来了。她们吃了Pollo Loco。

00:53:48.400 --> 00:54:15.020
<v Maricela>That day, it was her birthday. And I had to tell her that we were leaving. But her brother-- her brother knew before her, but we were supposed to surprise her. But when we were singing Happy Birthday, he told her. And then her eyes got kind of watery.
<v Maricela>那天是她的生日。我必须告诉她我们要离开了。但她哥哥——她哥哥比她先知道，我们本打算给她个惊喜。但当我们唱生日快乐歌时，他告诉了她。然后她的眼睛变得有些湿润。

00:54:15.020 --> 00:54:16.490
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>What about you?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你呢？

00:54:16.490 --> 00:54:18.710
<v Maricela>I wanted to cry.
<v Maricela>我想哭。

00:54:18.710 --> 00:54:19.610
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Did you?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你哭了吗？

00:54:19.610 --> 00:54:22.010
<v Maricela>Yeah.
<v Maricela>是的。

00:54:22.010 --> 00:54:44.960
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Maricela told Valeria she'd see her soon, but she never did. Valeria's family had been trying to make it work in LA, but struggled in those early months of the pandemic, and decided to move back to Ciudad Juarez. That was the last time they saw each other.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Maricela告诉Valeria她很快会再见到她，但她再也没见到。Valeria的家人一直试图在洛杉矶维持生计，但在大流行初期挣扎，决定搬回华雷斯城。那是她们最后一次见面。

00:54:44.960 --> 00:54:47.950
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>How does it feel to walk through the halls now?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>现在走在走廊里感觉如何？

00:54:47.950 --> 00:54:49.740
<v Maricela>OK.
<v Maricela>还行。

00:54:49.740 --> 00:55:14.460
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Knowing what the last year and a half was for Maricela, that it was not a blip, but a long time for a 12-year-old, full of huge experiences, I consider how brave it is what she's doing-- returning to this place that disappeared from her life, coming back after losing family members, her apartment, moving between countries, returning without knowing anything about what she's missed and without Valeria.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>知道过去一年半对Maricela意味着什么，这不是一个“闪现”，而是一个12岁孩子经历的漫长时光，充满了巨大的经历，我考虑到她所做的事情是多么勇敢——回到这个从她生活中消失的地方，在失去家人、公寓、国家间搬迁后回来，在不知道错过了什么的情况下回来，而且没有Valeria。

00:55:14.460 --> 00:55:29.460
<v Maricela>I was nervous, scared. I was like nervous, like, who I will see here. I go to the school, and then I leave. And then I come back, and they just stare at you the whole time. And I get nervous when they stare at me.
<v Maricela>我很紧张，害怕。我紧张得想知道我会在这里见到谁。我去学校，然后离开。然后我回来，他们只是盯着你看。他们盯着我看时我很紧张。

00:55:29.460 --> 00:55:30.750
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>You get nervous when they stare at you?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>他们盯着你看时你感到紧张？

00:55:30.750 --> 00:55:32.430
<v Maricela>Mm-hmm.
<v Maricela>嗯哼。

00:55:32.430 --> 00:55:33.150
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Yeah.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>是的。

00:55:33.150 --> 00:55:34.630
<v Maricela>It's, like, weird.
<v Maricela>这感觉很奇怪。

00:55:34.630 --> 00:55:37.170
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>What does it feel like?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>感觉是什么样子的？

00:55:37.170 --> 00:55:41.280
<v Maricela>It feels like a bunch of cameras watching me.
<v Maricela>感觉就像有一堆摄像头在盯着我。

00:55:41.280 --> 00:55:52.260
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>It does kind of seem like that. I watch as Maricela moves through the rest of her school day. She gets a lot of stares. She looks very nervous and very lost.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>看起来确实有点那样。我看着Maricela在学校度过剩下的时光。她受到了很多注视。她看起来非常紧张，非常迷失。

00:55:52.260 --> 00:55:57.990
<v Teacher>People were accusing Hamilton of being what's called a monarchist. Remember King George III?
<v Teacher>人们指责汉密尔顿是所谓的“保皇党”。记得乔治三世国王吗？

00:55:57.990 --> 00:56:11.610
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>In history class, the teacher does a lot of, remember when we learned about blah, blah, blah? Like, who can tell me what we know about the monarchy? Who remembers? The elites-- what do we mean by elites? You guys remember? Maricela, of course, does not remember.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>在历史课上，老师讲了很多，还记得我们学过的blah blah blah吗？比如，谁能告诉我我们对君主制了解多少？谁记得？精英——我们说的精英是什么意思？你们记得吗？Maricela当然不记得。

00:56:11.610 --> 00:56:17.220
<v Teacher 2>OK, so we're going to do quite a bit of reading today. All right. 109, Alabama, is everybody there?
<v Teacher 2>好的，我们今天要做大量的阅读。好的，109，阿拉巴马州，大家都在那儿吗？

00:56:17.220 --> 00:56:35.640
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>In English class, they read a novel written in verse, and then they have to write a response on an online platform. Maricela can't figure out how to submit her response. She's frustrated, but does not ask for help, does not know about the monarchy. She does not know how to use the online learning platform, and she does not speak to anyone.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>在英语课上，他们阅读一部诗体小说，然后必须在在线平台上写回复。Maricela没法弄清楚如何提交她的回复。她感到沮丧，但没有寻求帮助，她不知道关于君主制的事。她不知道如何使用在线学习平台，她没有和任何人说话。

00:56:35.640 --> 00:56:49.580
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>She's here. She's finally in the building, but she's still really far away. I felt that deeply, watching her in math. They're playing a game. Everyone has to get up and split it into two groups, but Maricela doesn't move.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>她来了。她终于在楼里了，但她依然非常遥远。在数学课上看着她时，我深深地感受到了这一点。他们在玩游戏。每个人都必须站起来分成两组，但Maricela没动。

00:56:49.580 --> 00:57:09.160
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>She's sitting in the back row, and she stays completely still, backpack propped on her desk, looking panicked as the other kids get up and sort themselves into teams. She's wearing a mic clipped to her shirt. She's too far from anyone else for them to hear what she's saying, but I can.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>她坐在最后一排，一动不动，背包架在桌子上，当其他孩子站起来分成小组时，她看起来很恐慌。她衣服上夹着一个麦克风。她离其他人太远，他们听不到她在说什么，但我能听到。

00:57:09.160 --> 00:57:12.360
<v Maricela>[GROANS] My stomach hurts.
<v Maricela>（呻吟）我肚子疼。

00:57:12.360 --> 00:57:21.030
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>The teacher notices that Maricela hasn't moved. And for the first time in hours, someone addresses her directly, tells her, you too. Come on.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>老师注意到Maricela没动。这是几小时来第一次有人直接跟她说话，告诉她，你也是。来吧。

00:57:21.030 --> 00:57:25.080
<v Teacher 3>You, too, pick a group. This one or that one?
<v Teacher 3>你也是，选个组。这个还是那个？

00:57:25.080 --> 00:57:27.390
<v Maricela>What if I can't play?
<v Maricela>如果我不能玩怎么办？

00:57:27.390 --> 00:57:29.040
<v Teacher 3>You can play. It's just math.
<v Teacher 3>你能玩。这只是数学。

00:57:29.040 --> 00:57:43.780
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>It's just math, the teacher says. But it is clearly not just math to Maricela. I keep waiting for someone to talk to her, to ask her something. What's going on with you? Where were you? What do you need?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>这只是数学，老师说。但这对于Maricela来说显然不仅仅是数学。我一直在等有人跟她说话，问她点什么。你发生什么事了？你去哪儿了？你需要什么？

00:57:43.780 --> 00:57:59.370
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>But school, day-to-day school, is not really set up for that. Her teachers will assess where Maricela is academically. And there's an aide in classes that could help her one-on-one, sometimes. But mostly, school is like this.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>但学校，日复一日的学校，并没有为此做好准备。她的老师会评估Maricela学术上的水平。班里有助教可以提供一对一的帮助，有时。但大多数时候，学校是这样的。

00:57:59.370 --> 00:58:12.560
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>This interaction with the math teacher, it lasts 11 seconds. She locks her eyes on Maricela, Maricela shakes her head. And then another kid jumps in front of the teacher, and the room of 25 people moves forward.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>这位数学老师的互动，持续了11秒。她盯着Maricela，Maricela摇了摇头。然后另一个孩子跳到老师面前，25个人的房间继续前进。

00:58:12.560 --> 00:58:22.760
<v Teacher 3>So I'm going to give you a question. Whoever answers the question first gets to come up here and write there, either their circle or their X. OK?
<v Teacher 3>所以我要给你们一个问题。谁先回答问题，谁就可以上来写，不管是圆还是X。好的？

00:58:22.760 --> 00:58:44.940
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>School is a machine that is designed to move forward. Kids move class-to-class, grade-to-grade. The machine does not stop. It's not designed to go back in time, to meet Maricela where she's at right now, which is at the back of the classroom, hiding behind a backpack, as her classmates enthusiastically compete to solve a math equation.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>学校是一个旨在不断向前的机器。孩子从课到课，年级到年级。机器不会停止。它不是为了回到过去而设计的，不是为了在此时此地满足Maricela的，而她现在就在教室后面，躲在背包后面，而她的同学们正热情地竞争解决一道数学题。

00:58:44.940 --> 00:58:50.930
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>[STUDENTS YELLING EXCITEDLY]
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>（学生兴奋地大叫）

00:58:50.930 --> 00:59:10.650
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Out of all the awkward moments I saw that day, this one was the hardest to watch, because you can feel the conveyor belt of school moving forward. I could see Maricela's panic that she could not figure out how to jump on.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>在那天我看到的所有尴尬时刻中，这一个是观看起来最困难的，因为你能感觉到学校的输送带在向前移动。我能看到Maricela无法弄清楚如何跳上输送带时的恐慌。

00:59:10.650 --> 00:59:25.990
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>And then, I see her try. Right before lunch, Maricela's standing in the hallway nervously digging through her backpack, other kids streaming past her to the lunch tables outside.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>然后，我看到她尝试了。就在午饭前，Maricela紧张地在走廊里翻找她的背包，其他孩子从她身边涌向外面的午餐桌。

00:59:25.990 --> 00:59:30.060
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>And then, all of a sudden, she calls out to another kid.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>然后，突然之间，她对着另一个孩子喊道。

00:59:30.060 --> 00:59:32.210
<v Maricela>Arecilli, mira.
<v Maricela>Arecilli, mira.

00:59:32.210 --> 00:59:52.220
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>She says, Arecilli, look, and opens up her bag. Arecilli is a tall, quiet girl in pink, who's been moving through the whole day in a pack of three-- three girls who, I'm told, have all recently arrived at the school from Mexico. Maricela starts showing Arecilli all the candy, and snacks, and lotion in her backpack.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>她说，Arecilli，你看，然后打开了她的包。Arecilli是一个穿粉色衣服、个子高高、安静的女孩，整天都在和另外两个女孩一组——我被告知，她们都是最近刚从墨西哥来到学校的。Maricela开始向Arecilli展示她背包里的所有糖果、零食和乳液。

00:59:52.220 --> 01:00:02.340
<v Maricela>Oh, look, and I have these. And I have-- look, and I have these. I have Bath and Body Works, too. [LAUGHS]
<v Maricela>哦，看，我有这些。还有——看，我有这些。我还有Bath and Body Works的。（大笑）

01:00:02.340 --> 01:00:16.380
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Now, the three girls are all leaning in over her backpack, giggling and slowly moving through the hall toward lunch up ahead of me. And a sixth-grader quickly replaces Maricela at my side, tells me she's been on TV, so I might recognize her.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>现在，三个女孩都凑在她的背包上方，咯咯笑着，慢慢穿过大厅走向午餐，在我前面。一个六年级学生迅速取代了Maricela站在我身边，告诉我她上过电视，所以我也许会认出她。

01:00:16.380 --> 01:00:20.340
<v Student>Have you seen a commercial where a dad's fixing a purple Jeep with his daughter?
<v Student>你看过一个爸爸和女儿修理紫色吉普车的广告吗？

01:00:20.340 --> 01:00:21.630
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>No. Is that you?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>没有。那是你吗？

01:00:21.630 --> 01:00:22.470
<v Student>Yeah.
<v Student>是的。

01:00:22.470 --> 01:00:23.250
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>You're the daughter?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你是那个女儿？

01:00:23.250 --> 01:00:30.690
<v Student>Yeah. And do you know the show, Henry Danger? OK. [LAUGHS]
<v Student>是的。你知道《亨利危险》那个节目吗？好的。（大笑）

01:00:30.690 --> 01:00:52.960
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>After disappointing this child star, I spot Maricela outside. She's in line for lunch, and she's with Arecilli and her friends. They're a nervous-looking pack, looking around like something bad could happen, not really talking. But they're a pack. Maricela seems OK for the first time in the whole day, actually, excited.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>在让这个童星失望后，我在外面发现了Maricela。她正在排队吃午饭，和Arecilli还有她的朋友在一起。她们是一群看起来很紧张的小团体，四处张望好像坏事会发生一样，并没有怎么说话。但她们是一个团体。Maricela看起来第一次一整天都还好，实际上，很兴奋。

01:00:52.960 --> 01:00:57.610
<v Maricela>Hanging out with Arecilli-- she's like Valeria.
<v Maricela>和Arecilli待在一起——她就像Valeria。

01:00:57.610 --> 01:00:58.400
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Really?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>真的吗？

01:00:58.400 --> 01:01:01.470
<v Maricela>Mm-hmm. They speak the same.
<v Maricela>嗯哼。她们说话一样。

01:01:01.470 --> 01:01:03.450
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Like, the way that they speak sounds the same?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>比如，她们说话的方式听起来一样？

01:01:03.450 --> 01:01:05.790
<v Maricela>Mm-hmm. And they kind of look the same.
<v Maricela>嗯哼。她们看起来也差不多。

01:01:05.790 --> 01:01:06.060
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Really?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>真的吗？

01:01:06.060 --> 01:01:20.250
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>It seems to me like an effort to jump back on the conveyor belt, that Maricela's trying to replicate what she had here before that mattered to her, trying to make a new school friend, who apparently is not dissimilar to her old school friend.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>在我看来，这像是跳回输送带的一次尝试，Maricela正试图复制她在这里曾经拥有的重要的东西，试图结交一个新学校朋友，看起来和她以前的学校朋友并没有什么不同。

01:01:20.250 --> 01:01:22.220
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Arecilli looks like her?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Arecilli看起来像她吗？

01:01:22.220 --> 01:01:25.300
<v Maricela>Mm-hmm. It was the tall, skinny girl that was with me right now.
<v Maricela>嗯哼。就是刚才跟我在一起的那个又高又瘦的女孩。

01:01:25.300 --> 01:01:27.280
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Do you think you guys will become as close?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>你认为你们会变得那么亲密吗？

01:01:27.280 --> 01:01:39.640
<v Maricela>Mm, I don't know, because, we're already in eighth grade. And then, when she leaves, I'm going to feel alone.
<v Maricela>嗯，我不知道，因为，我们已经在八年级了。然后，当她离开时，我会感到孤独。

01:01:39.640 --> 01:01:41.630
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>But you'd have eighth grade together.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>但你们会有在一起的八年级。

01:01:41.630 --> 01:01:43.930
<v Maricela>Mm.
<v Maricela>嗯。

01:01:43.930 --> 01:01:49.210
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>So you don't want to become close to her because, after eighth grade, you might not be together anymore?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>所以你不想和她变得亲密是因为，八年级之后，你们可能就不在一起了？

01:01:49.210 --> 01:01:53.600
<v Maricela>Mm-hmm. That's why.
<v Maricela>嗯哼。就是这样。

01:01:53.600 --> 01:02:07.190
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>I get it. She can't go back. They can't be as close, because Maricela missed most of middle school. And middle school is almost over. She can't go back to sixth-grade math, just like she can't go back to her apartment.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>我明白了。她回不去了。她们不可能那么亲密，因为Maricela错过了大部分初中。而且初中快结束了。她不能回到六年级的数学课，就像她不能回到她的公寓一样。

01:02:07.190 --> 01:02:19.880
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>And she definitely can't go back to Valeria. Everything is moving forward without her. Maricela watches Valeria online now, becoming a teenager without her.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>她绝对不能回到Valeria身边。一切都在没有她的情况下向前移动。Maricela现在在线看着Valeria，在没有她的情况下变成了青少年。

01:02:19.880 --> 01:02:25.760
<v Maricela>I see her, like-- I see her stories, and she looks, like, way different.
<v Maricela>我看着她，比如——我看着她的动态，她看起来，完全不同了。

01:02:25.760 --> 01:02:27.470
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Really?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>真的吗？

01:02:27.470 --> 01:02:38.450
<v Maricela>Like, she had, like, a little bit of freckles here, and they disappeared. And she had, like-- she put a nose piercing on. She's gonna-- I think she's gonna turn, like, 15.
<v Maricela>比如，她曾经有一点雀斑，现在消失了。她有——她打了鼻环。我想她要——我想她要15岁了。

01:02:38.450 --> 01:02:41.860
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>What does it feel like to see her looking different?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>看到她看起来不同了感觉如何？

01:02:41.860 --> 01:03:15.030
<v Maricela>Um, it feels weird. She, like, dresses different. She used to wear, like, long sleeves and jeans. And now she wears, like, really ripped jeans. And she wears, like, cropped tops now. Actually, it's like, I miss her.
<v Maricela>嗯，感觉很奇怪。她穿得不同了。她以前穿，比如，长袖和牛仔裤。现在她穿，比如，真的很破的牛仔裤。她现在穿露脐上衣。实际上，我，我想她了。

01:03:15.030 --> 01:03:38.400
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>I don't know how schools are going to fit in kids like Maricela. There are so many of them-- not just the millions of kids who have become chronically absent or disappeared entirely, but the tens of millions of kids who fell behind in math and reading, the millions of kids suffering from anxiety, trauma, grief. What happens if they don't fit back in?
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>我不知道学校该如何容纳像Maricela这样的孩子。她们有很多——不仅仅是数百万长期缺勤或完全消失的孩子，还有数千万在数学和阅读方面落后的孩子，数百万遭受焦虑、创伤、悲伤的孩子。如果她们没法融入回来会怎样？

01:03:38.400 --> 01:03:52.320
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Maricela has been coming to school for six months now, but she doesn't always come. Her attendance is pretty spotty. Principal Vanessa Garza tells me Maricela is now three grades behind, but she will be promoted to ninth grade.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>Maricela来学校已经六个月了，但她不总是来。她的出勤率很不稳定。Vanessa Garza校长告诉我Maricela现在落后三个年级，但她将被升入九年级。

01:03:52.320 --> 01:04:09.600
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>She won't be able to walk at graduation because of the attendance issues, but Ms. Vanessa thinks the shame of being held back would be the end of school for Maricela. And she has a better shot of finishing high school, if she can start earning credits toward graduation now. She'll keep moving forward.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>由于出勤问题她没法参加毕业典礼，但Vanessa女士认为留级的羞辱对于Maricela来说将是学校生活的终点。如果她现在能开始赚取通往毕业的学分，她更有机会完成高中。她会继续向前。

01:04:09.600 --> 01:04:50.560
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>I asked Maricela if she likes being back in school. She said, no, but she's going to keep trying.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>我问Maricela她喜欢回到学校吗。她说，不喜欢，但她会继续努力。

